    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eb30e5f6_d231737c",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 6158,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-22T12:05:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ISTM that if Passpoint supplies a URL, then either the AP should not be Capport-enabled or the Capport API should return the same URL.\n\nGenerally I think we want to encourage vendors to use Capport rather than Passpoint because of its improved generality and openness, so if the URLs are both non-null and different I think we should probably in fact prefer the Capport URL. Even if the Capport API is present but has a null URL I think we may not want to display the Passpoint URL to encourage vendors to correctly fill their Capport API fields (of course if the Capport API is not present at all we should use Passpoint).\n\nThoughts ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6156,
        "startChar": 66,
        "endLine": 6158,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "01f3d2b03e4a7867028da02dd8dbbe002212a599",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d8a685e_0f22da23",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 6158,
      "author": {
        "id": 1480931
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-23T01:24:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually - no. \n\nWe want to encourage vendors to use Passpoint rather than Capport. Passpoint is the Wi-Fi technology moving forward which is secure and allows for large scale federated roaming and carrier offload to Wi-Fi. The URLs retrieved by Passpoint cannot be spoofed by an attacker and therefore trusted.\n\nSo I disagree with your assessment, and Passpoint must take precedence.\nGoogle \"OpenRoaming\" and \"Orion Wi-Fi\". The latter is a Google project. Google Fi also uses Passpoint.",
      "parentUuid": "eb30e5f6_d231737c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6156,
        "startChar": 66,
        "endLine": 6158,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "01f3d2b03e4a7867028da02dd8dbbe002212a599",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
